  "summary": "A calligraphic practice emphasizing dynamic line energy and brush movement during New Year writing.",
  "description": "Kakizome features bold, expressive brushstrokes that demonstrate the calligrapher's energy and skill, with varying line weights and speeds creating rhythmic compositions. This tradition originated in Japan's imperial court during the Heian Period as a New Year ritual, where auspicious characters were written to set positive intentions for the coming year, embodying the spiritual connection between brush movement and cosmic energy.",
